  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1104 AM CDT Fri May 29 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging begins to build over the Plains starting Sunday. \nWhile drier air will begin to work its way into Middle TN in \nresponse, enough moisture will linger to keep low to medium rain \nchances in the forecast through Monday. We finally get at least a\nfew dry days Tuesday through Thursday as the upper-level ridge \ndominates the pattern and its axis slowly shifts east. Low rain \nchances look to return on Friday as models hint that the ridge \nbreaks down with moisture returning to the area. As we make our \nway into June, look for highs to generally be in the low to \nmid-80s which is near normal.",
